From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "pocketforge-agent[bot]"
 <299760760+pocketforge-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 08:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] hw/misc: model A133 LEDC transfer status

Model the LED controller so release-guest PIO transfers complete: DATA
writes fill a 32-word FIFO, a virtual-clock timer consumes one word per
tick at the rate implied by T01_TIMING, and TRANS_FINISH and
FIFO_CPUREQ latch into the write-one-to-clear INT_STS, which also
reports FIFO_WLW. The level IRQ on GIC SPI 35 is raised when a latched
status bit is enabled and GLOBAL_INT_EN is set. Clearing LEDC_EN aborts
the transfer, flushes the FIFO and clears the latched status. The
decoded per-LED colours are readable from the read-only "led-colors"
string property at /machine/pocketforge-ledc.

RGB_MODE only orders the bytes on the wire; the release driver always
packs words as 0x00RRGGBB (drivers/leds/leds-sun50i-a100.c:226-228),
so the decode is mode independent. The DMA path is unreachable in this
machine model: the driver uses DMA only for transfers longer than the
32-word FIFO (leds-sun50i-a100.c:149) while the release DT registers 23
LEDs. DMA_CTRL is stored for read-back and for the FIFO trigger level
that FIFO_CPUREQ latching uses.

The aperture leaves the inert stub list, so the MMIO map test now
counts LEDC as modelled.

